# A block written in place (scenes/parts.seed.ts writes the note into a scratch outline): found by its title, opened
# to be written, and typed in, with a note's name begun, so the service's list of what completes it hangs at the
# caret. Then an agent tidies the paragraph above, through the service: it lands in the draft in front of the
# person, lit, and the tile says who changed what. The saved note is untouched until the person saves.
bar.open scope=search query="Frost fleece"
bar.pick n=1
edit
draft.paste text=" It lives in the ((Pott"
draft.patch observed="trays  on a cold  night" replacement="trays on a cold night" as=tidy-agent
